# Every text file checks out as LF in the working tree (as Prettier wants with
# `endOfLine: lf`): without this line, core.autocrlf converts them to CRLF on
# Windows and `npm run format:check` fails on every file. The exceptions below
# still win because they are more specific and declared later.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Scripts executed by cmd.exe require CRLF line endings: with LF only, the cmd
# parser drops the first character of commands after label jumps/goto.
# `text eol=crlf` = LF stays normalized in the repository, while the working
# tree ALWAYS extracts CRLF (regardless of core.autocrlf).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
